  "body": "### Summary\nAs the maintainer, I want the three older stores to follow the same load rules as `SmallStoreState`, so that \"update the app\" is told apart from \"file damaged\", an empty account is refused, and one account has one key whatever its spelling. The duplication itself is for #836; the diverging behaviour is the finding.\n\n### Scenarios\n1. A v2 pseudo-list or reading-positions file whose shape changed is reported as `loadFailed(<decoding error>)` instead of `unsupportedVersion(2)`.\n2. `block(\"x\", account: \"\")` stores a blocklist under the key `\"\"`.\n3. Positions recorded under \"Alice\" are not found under \"alice\" (the app already works around it).\n\n### Evidence (`7a61018f`)\n- `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRStorage/SmallStores/Core/FileSmallStorePersistence.swift:24-27`: reads the version first (\"a newer format may not decode as this one, and must still be reported as newer\") and refuses `version < 1`.\n- `PseudoLists/FilePseudoListPersistence.swift:17-20` and `ReadingPositions/FileReadingPositionPersistence.swift:17-20` decode the whole document directly.\n- `PseudoLists/PseudoListStore.swift:70`: `document.blocklists[AccountKey.make(account), default: []]` with no empty-account check (small stores use `AccountKey.forWriting`, which throws `.emptyAccount`).\n- `ReadingPositions/ReadingPositionStore.swift:38,43,82,100,180`: `document.accounts[account]` by the raw string; `App/SwiftHFR/Accounts/AccountDataEraser.swift:99-106` removes \"every spelling of the account's key\".\n\n### Fix\nMove the three stores onto `SmallStoreState` + `FileSmallStorePersistence` (file names, encoders and date strategies kept; positions keys migrated on read to `AccountKey`).\n\n### Tests (fail before the fix)\n- `FilePseudoListPersistenceTests/newerVersionWithAnotherShapeIsReportedAsNewer`: `{\"version\":2,\"lists\":{}}` gives `.unsupportedVersion(2)` (today `loadFailed`).\n- `ReadingPositionStoreTests/positionIsFoundWhateverTheAccountCase`.\n\nRework model: Sonnet 5.5, reviewed by Opus 5.5. Group with the storage family of #836.\n\nFound by #775 (cloud/r775-fable, Fable 5.2). Reviewed at `dev-swift` @ `7a61018f`; read from the code, not run on a device unless stated.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
