   "body": "/claim cloud/m4q-reliab-opus\n\nRe-checked on `dev-swift` @ bc3eeb36: all three scenarios still hold.\n- `FilePseudoListPersistence` and `FileReadingPositionPersistence` decode the whole document without reading the version first.\n- `PseudoListStore` writes blocklists under `AccountKey.make` with no empty check.\n- `ReadingPositionStore` uses the raw account string everywhere.\n\nNo open PR touches `PseudoLists/`, `ReadingPositions/` or their tests.\n\nPlan. The issue says the duplication itself is #836's, and the diverging behaviour is the finding here. So this PR brings the three guards into the existing stores instead of moving them onto `SmallStoreState`, which is a larger, riskier change better done with #836. File names, encoders and the v1 formats stay as they are.\n1. **Golden v1 files first.** Pseudo lists get a new literal file test. Positions already have one (`aRecordHoldsOnlyIdsAndNumbers`).\n2. **Version read first** (the shared probe of `FileSmallStorePersistence`): a newer version, whatever its shape, gives `unsupportedVersion(n)`; a version below 1 gives `loadFailed`. This applies to pseudo lists and positions. Drafts already set a newer file aside, whichever error, so their outcome does not change.\n3. **Empty account refused** on blocklist writes (`PseudoListError.emptyAccount`; the editor's message has a `default` branch). Positions already refuse an empty account.\n4. **Positions keyed by `AccountKey`.** Reads and writes use `AccountKey.make(account)`. Spellings stored before are merged on read: per topic the newest wins, as in `merge`. They are written under the key at the next save.\n5. **Tests**, red before the change: `newerVersionWithAnotherShapeIsReportedAsNewer` (both stores), `positionIsFoundWhateverTheAccountCase`, `spellingsStoredBeforeAreMergedOnRead`, `anEmptyAccountIsRefused`.\n6. Draft PR, then a Fable review.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
